# Architecture

## Layers

| Path | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `src/api/` | HTTP client, Bearer header, `getMessages` / `createMessage`, typed errors |
| `src/types/` | Shared domain types matching the API |
| `src/hooks/` | Data orchestration (`useMessages`); no raw `fetch` in components |
| `src/components/` | Presentational UI only |
| `src/config/env.ts` | Sole place that reads `import.meta.env` |
| `src/styles/` | Global tokens and layout |
| `e2e/` | Playwright specs |

## Rules

- Keep architecture shallow: a few clear folders, not deep trees.
- No business/API logic inside presentational components.
- Current user is `VITE_CURRENT_AUTHOR`; outgoing UI when `author === currentAuthor`.
- App must remain a static Vite build (`dist/`) so it can be served by nginx later.
- Prefer plain CSS + variables over heavy UI libraries or CSS-in-JS.
- No Redux or global state libraries — React state + hooks.
